<section class="about" id="about">
  <div class="wrap about-grid">
    <div class="about-visual">
      <div class="about-photo">
        <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/7534561/pexels-photo-7534561.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Living room interior, Agam Estates residence">
        <span class="about-photo-caption">Sample residence interior · indicative finish</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT AGAM ESTATES</div>
      <p class="lead">We build few projects at a time, so that each one gets the attention a home deserves.</p>
      <p>Agam Estates is a Tricity-based developer working across Panchkula, Zirakpur and the Ambala corridor. Our approach starts with the land — its orientation, its shade, the way morning light should fall through a living room — before a single unit plan is drawn.</p>
      <p>Every residence carries Mivan shear-wall construction, RCC-framed balconies and double-glazed façades, delivered with the same project team from groundbreaking to handover.</p>
      <div class="signature-line">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 52 52" fill="none"><circle cx="26" cy="26" r="25" stroke="#DDAE45"/><path d="M16 30L23 22L29 27L36 18" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>
        <div>
          <strong>Founded on a single promise</strong>
          <span>Design first, deliver on date, stand behind the build.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="partners" id="developers">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="partner-head">
      <h2>Builders and developers we vouch for.</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--fade); font-size:0.9rem; max-width:280px;">Beyond our own residences, our advisory desk works directly with these established regional builders — no intermediaries, no inflated pricing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="partner-grid">
      <div class="partner-card">
        <div class="partner-photo"><img src="https://sales-test1.process360.us/images/image1.png" alt="Northgate Realty project exterior"></div>
        <span class="partner-region">MOHALI · ZIRAKPUR</span>
        <h3>Northgate Realty</h3>
        <p>Fourteen years across residential floors and gated plots, with a reputation for handing over exactly what was shown in the brochure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="partner-card">
        <div class="partner-photo"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/39520071/pexels-photo-39520071.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=700" alt="Silverleaf Developers township exterior"></div>
        <span class="partner-region">NEW CHANDIGARH</span>
        <h3>Silverleaf Developers</h3>
        <p>Integrated townships built around retained tree cover and shared courtyards — a favourite with buyers who want scale without density.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="partner-card">
        <div class="partner-photo"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/38197605/pexels-photo-38197605.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=700" alt="Crestline Group residential exterior"></div>
        <span class="partner-region">PANCHKULA</span>
        <h3>Crestline Group</h3>
        <p>Low-rise, low-density independent floors on wide sector roads — the choice for buyers prioritising privacy over height.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="partner-card">
        <div class="partner-photo"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/16072809/pexels-photo-16072809.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=700" alt="Aurelia Homes residential exterior"></div>
        <span class="partner-region">KHARAR · MOHALI</span>
        <h3>Aurelia Homes</h3>
        <p>Value-corridor apartments and plots aimed at long-horizon investors, backed by a construction pace they publish every quarter.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="partner-card">
        <div class="partner-photo"><img src="https://sales-test1.process360.us/images/image2.png" alt="Kingswood Estates project exterior"></div>
        <span class="partner-region">SECTOR BELT · MOHALI</span>
        <h3>Kingswood Estates</h3>
        <p>SCOs, commercial floors and mixed-use blocks along the main sector arteries, delivered on a track record of on-time possession.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="partner-card">
        <div class="partner-photo"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/30987933/pexels-photo-30987933.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=700" alt="Meridian Group residential portfolio"></div>
        <span class="partner-region">TRICITY-WIDE</span>
        <h3>Meridian Group</h3>
        <p>A multi-city portfolio spanning residential towers, retail and light industrial — one of the region's most diversified builders.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pillars on-dark" id="pillars">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHY AGAM</div>
      <h2>What you're actually paying for</h2>
      <p class="fade-text">Three things separate a good address from a good home — we design around all three, not just the one that photographs well.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pillar-grid">
      <div class="pillar">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none"><path d="M4 18L17 6L30 18" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M8 16V29H26V16" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>
        <h3>A campus, not a compound</h3>
        <p>6.2 acres with a 60% open landscape ratio — towers are set back and staggered so no two homes look directly into another.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none"><rect x="6" y="6" width="22" height="22" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M6 14H28M14 6V28" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg>
        <h3>Real plan efficiency</h3>
        <p>No wasted lobbies or dead corners — carpet-to-super-area ratios are published upfront, unit by unit, before you book.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none"><path d="M17 4V30M6 17H28" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.4"/><circle cx="17" cy="17" r="12" stroke="#DDAE45" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg>
        <h3>Ten minutes to everything</h3>
        <p>Positioned between the Panchkula and Zirakpur growth corridors, with the airport, PGI and IT hubs all under twenty minutes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="location" id="location">
  <div class="wrap loc-layout">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">THE ADDRESS</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,3.4vw,2.6rem); margin-top:14px; line-height:1.15;">Close to the Tricity, away from its noise</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--fade); margin-top:18px; max-width:420px;">Sector 20, Panchkula Extension sits just off the Kalka–Zirakpur highway — near enough for a daily commute, far enough for the drive home to feel like an exhale.</p>
      <div class="loc-filter" id="loc-filter">
        <button class="active" data-filter="all">All</button>
        <button data-filter="transit">Transit</button>
        <button data-filter="education">Education</button>
        <button data-filter="health">Health &amp; Retail</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="loc-list" id="loc-list">
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="transit"><span class="tag">Transit</span><h4>Chandigarh International Airport</h4><span class="time">18 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="transit"><span class="tag">Transit</span><h4>Panchkula Railway Station</h4><span class="time">9 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="education"><span class="tag">Education</span><h4>DAV &amp; DPS School Cluster</h4><span class="time">6 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="education"><span class="tag">Education</span><h4>Chitkara University</h4><span class="time">15 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="health"><span class="tag">Health</span><h4>PGI Chandigarh</h4><span class="time">22 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="health"><span class="tag">Health</span><h4>Alchemist &amp; Fortis Hospitals</h4><span class="time">10 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="health"><span class="tag">Retail</span><h4>Elante Mall &amp; VR Punjab</h4><span class="time">17 min</span></div>
      <div class="loc-item" data-cat="transit"><span class="tag">Transit</span><h4>ISBT Sector 43</h4><span class="time">14 min</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="residences on-dark" id="residences">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">RESIDENCES</div>
      <h2>Three layouts, one standard</h2>
      <p class="fade-text">Every plan below carries the same finish specification — the difference is only how much space you want to live in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="plan-tabs" id="plan-tabs">
      <button class="plan-tab active" data-plan="p1">3 BHK · 1,620 sq ft</button>
      <button class="plan-tab" data-plan="p2">3 BHK + Study · 2,040 sq ft</button>
      <button class="plan-tab" data-plan="p3">4 BHK · 2,780 sq ft</button>
    </div>

    <div class="plan-panel active" id="p1">
      <div class="plan-photo"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/7534561/pexels-photo-7534561.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=900" alt="3 BHK living room, sample interior"></div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="color:var(--light); font-size:1.6rem; margin-bottom:14px;">Compact, correctly.</h3>
        <p style="color:#C6D0E0; max-width:420px;">A cross-ventilated layout with a private utility balcony off the kitchen and a foyer that keeps the living room from opening straight onto the front door.</p>
        <div class="plan-specs">
          <div><strong>1,620</strong><span>Sq ft super area</span></div>
          <div><strong>3</strong><span>Bedrooms, 3 baths</span></div>
          <div><strong>2</strong><span>Reserved car bays</span></div>
          <div><strong>N-E</strong><span>Facing available</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="plan-panel" id="p2">
      <div class="plan-photo"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/7534554/pexels-photo-7534554.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=900" alt="3 BHK plus study living area, sample interior"></div>
